How to make a deep copy of the `Net` object?

I am not able to think of any straightforward way to do this. This is one option:

```
Net nets[2];
for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++)
{
    Net& net = nets[i];
    int convId = net.addLayer(convParams.name, convParams.type, convParams);
    int eltwiseId = net.addLayer(eltwiseParams.name, eltwiseParams.type, eltwiseParams);
    int activeId = net.addLayer(activationParams.name, activationParams.type, activationParams);
    net.connect(0, 0, convId, 0);
    net.connect(convId, 0, eltwiseId, 0);
    net.connect(0, 0, eltwiseId, 1);
    net.connect(eltwiseId, 0, activeId, 0);
}
```

`TestLayerFusion::test` would take two `Net&` as input.
